Third-party code
----------------
None yet. When code is copied or ported from another project, add a
line at the top of this file in this form, with the holder and years
worded as that project words them:

    Portions Copyright <their years> <their name> (in respect of lines
    taken from the <Project> project)

Then record the rest here: the
project, its licence, the contents of its own NOTICE file if it has one,
and which aeo files carry the derived code. Each such file also keeps the
original copyright notice and states that it was changed.

Apache-2.0 and MIT/BSD sources may be brought in on those terms. GPL or
AGPL sources (Ansible, for one) may not.
